## 6. Excluded columns: a policy decision with a measured cost

`{{ ablation.columns|join("` and `") }}` are excluded from the features by manual policy (`leakage.policy = {{ ablation.policy }}`). This is a policy decision, not a demonstrated case of leakage.

| Column | abs. correlation with label | Detector limit |
|---|---|---|
{% for c in ablation.corr_rows %}| {{ c.column }} | {{ "%.3f"|format(c.abs_corr) }} | {{ "%.2f"|format(ablation.threshold) }} |
{% endfor %}
{% if ablation.detector_flagged %}The correlation detector flagged: {{ ablation.detector_flagged|join(", ") }}.{% else %}The correlation detector did not flag either column; the exclusion does not come from the detector.{% endif %}

The reason for excluding them is plausible: both accumulate over a customer's lifetime, and for a churner they stop at the point of churn, so a model that uses them partly measures how long customers stayed. This cannot be verified with this data, because it has no dates (no signup, snapshot, or churn date) from which to show when the values were measured relative to the prediction.

Cost of the policy, on the test set, over {{ ablation.n_seeds }} random splits (diagnostic only; the official model above does not use these columns):

